{
  "_comment": "PROPOSAL — NOT FROZEN. An APPEND-ONLY expansion of data/palette.json: c00-c31 are byte-identical to the frozen palette and only c32+ are new, so no existing slot changes meaning and no UI_SWATCH role needs re-pointing (the T-15 failure mode cannot occur). data/palette.json is untouched. Regenerate with `npx tsx assets/approved-trials/_palette-refreeze/expand.mjs` (deterministic, k-means++ seeded at 42 via core/rng.ts). Evidence in assets/approved-trials/_palette-refreeze/_fit-report.json.",
  "_method": {
    "algorithm": "augmenting weighted k-means: the frozen 32 are fixed centres, new centres are fitted only to the colour mass they serve worst; assignment is nearest-in-sRGB, exactly tools/postprocess/steps.ts::quantize",
    "determinism": "k-means++ seeded at 42 via core/rng.ts (no Math.random, G11); re-running reproduces colors[] byte-identically",
    "errorMetric": "CIEDE2000",
    "countDerivation": "candidates added one at a time by largest MEASURED marginal reduction in weighted mean ΔE2000; stopped when the best remaining candidate was worth less than 0.05. The count was not chosen.",
    "separationNote": "MIN_SEPARATION 5 is an anti-duplicate floor, NOT the redundancy test. A ΔE2000 separation threshold misfires in the dark end: #29272e is 7.8 ΔE from c30 #272940 yet is among the most valuable swatches available, because c30 is a navy and #29272e is neutral. Marginal value is measured directly instead.",
    "sourcesExcluded": {
      "assets/final/maps/**": "already quantized to the frozen palette (17-32 distinct colours measured) — fitting to these would fit the palette to itself",
      "assets/reference/**": "FORBIDDEN. Pokemon reference images, inspiration-only per assets/reference/README.md; deriving our palette from them would bake another game's palette into this one.",
      "assets/raw/_trials/topdown-examples/control-*.png": "ControlNet control images — black line art on white, 256 greyscale values, not colour art"
    }
  },
